  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
       ASSESSMENT
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="assessment" style="background:#fff1f0;padding:112px 0;">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:1200px;">
      <div style="margin-bottom:48px;">
        <div class="gk-eyebrow">The Assessment</div>
        <h2 class="gk-sh-title">Start by discovering what your evidence <span style="font-family:'Lora',serif;font-style:italic;font-weight:500;color:#FF5656;">can already support</span>.</h2>
        <p class="gk-sh-body" style="max-width:800px;">The Impact Reporting &amp; Data Readiness Assessment is the starting point for building your organization's evidence system. We focus on one or two priority programs and one immediate funder or reporting need.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="row g-4 align-items-stretch">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-6 d-flex">
          <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3e4e8;border-radius:14px;padding:28px;width:100%;">
            <h3 style="font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:17px;color:#283853;margin:0 0 14px;">The Assessment helps identify:</h3>
            <ul style="margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:'Roboto',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;color:#4d525e;line-height:1.9;">
              <li>Which information already supports your impact story</li>
              <li>Where evidence is difficult to find or reuse</li>
              <li>Where important claims are weak, incomplete, or unsupported</li>
              <li>What your team should begin capturing differently</li>
              <li>The most practical next steps for strengthening reporting readiness</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-6 d-flex">
          <div style="background:#283853;border-radius:14px;padding:28px;width:100%;display:flex;flex-direction:column;">
            <div style="font-family:'Roboto',sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#ff8c83;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px;">Current design-partner offer</div>
            <h3 style="font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:17px;color:#fff;margin:0 0 14px;line-height:1.35;">Get Kinder is inviting five BC nonprofits to participate as design partners and receive the Assessment at no cost.</h3>
            <p style="font-family:'Roboto',sans-serif;font-size:13.5px;color:#dfe3ec;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 8px;">The Assessment includes:</p>
            <ul style="margin:0 0 20px;padding-left:20px;font-family:'Roboto',sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:#dfe3ec;line-height:1.8;flex:1;">
              <li>An inventory of existing information and evidence sources</li>
              <li>A reporting-readiness scorecard</li>
              <li>A prioritized gap and risk list</li>
              <li>A review of the impact claims most important to the organization's funding goals</li>
              <li>Practical recommendations for improving future evidence capture</li>
              <li>A prioritized implementation roadmap</li>
              <li>A readout session with the Get Kinder team</li>
            </ul>
            <div><a href="/home/book" class="gk-cta-primary">Apply for a Reporting Readiness Call</a></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:32px;font-family:'Lora',serif;font-style:italic;font-weight:500;font-size:18px;color:#455A7C;max-width:640px;">The Assessment is not the final product. It is how your organization begins building a reusable evidence system.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:12px;font-family:'Roboto',sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:#6e7280;line-height:1.6;max-width:800px;">The Assessment provides independent value and does not commit the organization to purchasing anything afterward. Any continued work with Get Kinder is a separate decision.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
