  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="faq" style="background:#fff;padding:112px 0;">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:1200px;">
      <div class="row g-5">
        <!-- Left: sticky label -->
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-4">
          <div style="position:sticky;top:100px;">
            <div class="gk-eyebrow">FAQ</div>
            <h2 style="font-family:'Poppins',sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(26px,2.8vw,36px);letter-spacing:-0.02em;color:#455a7c;margin:0;line-height:1.18;">Questions nonprofits <span style="font-family:'Lora',serif;font-style:italic;font-weight:500;color:#FF5656;">usually ask first.</span></h2>
            <p style="margin-top:18px;font-family:'Roboto',sans-serif;font-size:15px;color:#4d525e;line-height:1.6;">Real questions from executive directors, development leads, and program directors we've spoken with.</p>
            <div style="margin-top:24px;">
              <a href="/home/book" style="font-family:'Roboto',sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:#FF5656;font-weight:500;text-decoration:none;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;">Still have a question? Book a call <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;color:#FF5656;"></i></a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <!-- Right: accordion -->
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-8">
          <% [
            {q:'How can a nonprofit prove its impact to funders?', a:'A nonprofit can make its impact more defensible by connecting each important claim to a specific source, clear definition, relevant reporting period, known limitations, and authorized human review. Get Kinder helps teams find that information across existing records, identify gaps before a deadline, and preserve approved evidence for future use. Get Kinder does not independently verify impact or guarantee a funder decision.'},
            {q:'How can a small nonprofit reduce grant-reporting workload?', a:'A nonprofit can reduce reporting workload by preserving reviewed evidence, definitions, source information, and approval decisions for reuse instead of reconstructing them for every report. Get Kinder helps organizations build that reusable evidence foundation while identifying a manageable number of evidence-capture practices that will make future reporting easier.'},
            {q:'What evidence do funders expect from nonprofits?', a:'There is no single evidence list that applies to every funder. Requirements commonly relate to funded activities, participation, outputs, observed outcomes, use of funds, reporting periods, and the sources supporting important claims. Get Kinder begins with the organization\'s actual funder template or reporting obligation so the evidence work reflects what that funder is requesting rather than a generic checklist.'},
            {q:'Do nonprofits need clean or perfectly organized data to use Get Kinder?', a:'No. Get Kinder is designed to begin with the reports, spreadsheets, records, surveys, and other information the organization already holds. The Assessment identifies what appears usable, what requires clarification, what is missing, and which evidence-capture practices should improve next. Human context and review are still required.'},
            {q:'What is the Impact Reporting & Data Readiness Assessment?', a:"The Impact Reporting & Data Readiness Assessment is Get Kinder's starting point for understanding what evidence a nonprofit already has, what its priority reporting need requires, where gaps and risks remain, and what should improve next. It focuses on one or two priority programs and creates the starting point for a reusable evidence system rather than ending as a disconnected report."},
            {q:'Is Get Kinder a grant-writing tool?', a:'No. Get Kinder starts before the writing by helping an organization understand, review, and preserve the evidence supporting its reports and applications. Evidence-grounded drafting may be supported where that capability is actually available, but Get Kinder should not be positioned as a generic AI grant writer or as a substitute for organizational judgment.'},
            {q:"Does KAI decide whether a nonprofit's impact claim is true?", a:'No. Kinder AI™ (KAI) does not independently determine organizational truth or approve impact claims. KAI is the AI built into the Knowledge Studio and can help users understand findings, identify gaps and inconsistencies, answer questions, and work with eligible evidence. Authorized humans remain responsible for interpretations, conclusions, approvals, and permitted uses.'},
            {q:"Can funders access a nonprofit's source information through Get Kinder?", a:"Not by default. A funder relationship does not create unrestricted access to a nonprofit's source files, sensitive records, or unapproved evidence. Any future portfolio reporting must use clearly defined permissions and information approved for that purpose and audience."}
          ].forEach(function(item, i) { %>
          <div class="<%= i === 0 ? 'gk-faq-first' : '' %>" style="border-bottom:1px solid #e3e4e8;">
            <button class="gk-faq-btn">
              <span style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;"><span style="font-family:'Roboto',sans-serif;font-size:11px;color:#9a9ea7;letter-spacing:0.08em;font-weight:600;width:28px;flex-shrink:0;"><%= String(i+1).padStart(2,'0') %></span><span style="line-height:1.4;"><%= item.q %></span></span>
              <span class="gk-faq-icon" style="background:#f1f3f7;"><i data-lucide="plus" style="width:14px;height:14px;color:#455A7C;"></i></span>
            </button>
            <div class="gk-faq-body" style="max-height:0px;"><div class="gk-faq-body-inner"><p><%= item.a %></p></div></div>
          </div>
          <% }); %>
          <p style="margin-top:20px;"><a href="/home/faq" style="font-family:'Roboto',sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:#FF5656;font-weight:500;text-decoration:none;">Read the full FAQ</a><span style="font-family:'Roboto',sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:#6e7280;"> — proving impact, responsible AI, and the Assessment in detail.</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

